  "note": "Verso body page that changes structure part way down. Blocks 1-10 are set to the FULL verso measure x 0.314-0.903 and are column 'full' (block 10's last line already narrows into the right column, which is why it is 'full' too). From y 0.709 the page is TWO columns: Figure 1.30 and its cyan caption occupy the OUTER (left) margin column x 0.130-0.470, with blocks 12 and 13 set in a narrow right column x 0.489-0.903; a clean empty gutter separates them at x 0.470-0.489. The figure caption has no A2 block and takes n: null; it is printed entirely in the chapter cyan #00adef. No fill is reported for the figure - the pale blue of the sheet and parallelepiped is artwork, not a panel tint. A naive saturated-row scan reports a light-blue band at y 0.622-0.629, x 0.712-0.783 (#c3ecfb); that is only the anti-aliased halo of the cyan section heading 1.15.2 on that row, NOT a printed band - it must not be read as a rule_bar. This page's only real coloured band is the page_header_band, the pale blue #c6eafb strip across the whole page top (y 0-0.067), whose #41c7f4 hairline and #00adef foot rule are internal edges of that one band. There is no rule_bar and no footer_rule on this page. '1.15.2 Field due to a uniformly charged infinite plane sheet' is cyan #00adef sans, the chapter's sub-heading colour. The '2022-23' edition line at the foot is recorded as a second running_header because the allowed role list has no footer-text role. All 13 A2 blocks matched by position."
